{"status": "ok", "backend": "ddgs-auto", "query": "Erythematous patch with peripheral scale groin rash in 17 yr old football player", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T19:24:41.295145+00:00", "documents": [{"title": "Tinea Cruris Clinical Presentation: History, Physical ...", "url": "https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1091806-clinical", "snippet": "Mar 17, 2025 · Tinea cruris manifests as a symmetric erythematous rash in the groin (see the images below). Large patches of erythema with central clearing are centered on the inguinal creases and..."}, {"title": "Pityriasis Rosea Clinical Presentation: History, Physical ...", "url": "https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1107532-clinical", "snippet": "Oct 1, 2026 · The herald patch usually shows a collarette of fine scales just inside its well-demarcated edges and may exhibit central clearing, much as in tinea corporis. This patch is something of a..."}, {"title": "Erythrasma: Symptoms, Causes, Treatment, and More - HealthlineErythrasma: Symptoms, Causes & Treatment - Cleveland ClinicErythrasma: What It Looks Like and How to Get Rid of ItErythrasma - The Primary Care Dermatology SocietyScaly skin diseases - DermNet", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/erythrasma", "snippet": "Erythrasma is a type of bacterial infection that may appear in folds of the skin. It’s often itchy and may have pink, red, or brown patches with scales. It’s more common in people with medical conditions that affect the immune system. Erythrasma is a bacterial infection that affects the skin. It usually appears in the folds of the skin. It’s more commonly seen in warm or humid climates and is usually caused by the bacteria Corynebacterium minutissimum. Erythrasma tends to be a chronic or long-term skin condition. See full list on healthline.com The most common symptoms of erythrasma include pink, red, or brown skin patches with scales, and mildly itchy skin. Sometimes the skin may also be wrinkled. The patches can vary in size, and usually start as a pink or red color. Then, they become brown and scaly. The patches typically appear in the folds of the skin and are more common in the groin area, armpits, or between the toes. When you have erythrasma between the toes, you may see fissures and scaly skin. Erythrasma can also appear in the skin folds under the breasts, between the buttocks, or around the navel. See full list on healthline.com Erythrasma is caused by the Corynebacterium minutissimum bacteria. The bacteria normally live on the skin and can grow in warm, moist areas. That’s why it’s commonly found in folds of the skin. See full list on healthline.com You’re more likely to develop erythrasma if you: •have diabetes •live in a warm or humid climate •sweat a lot •are obese •are older See full list on healthline.com Your doctor will ask you about your medical history and do a physical exam to start the diagnosis process. Then, your doctor will do a Wood’s lamp skin examination. This lamp uses ultraviolet radiation to look at your skin. Under this lamp, erythrasma will have a red or coral color. Your doctor may take a swab or skin scraping to examine the cultures more closely under a microscope. See full list on healthline.com Treatment will depend on the severity of your condition. Your doctor may recommend any of the following treatments: •oral antibiotics, such as erythromycin (Erythrocin Stearate) •cleaning the affected area with antibiotic soap •applying fusidic acid to the skin •antibacterial solutions or creams on your skin, such as clindamycin HCL solution, erythromycin cream, or miconazole cream (Lotrimin, Cruex) •red light therapy See full list on healthline.com Complications are rare with erythrasma. In rare cases, erythrasma can become more serious. Septicemia, a serious blood infection, may develop. See full list on healthline.com There are several things you may be able to do to prevent erythrasma: •Keep your skin dry and clean. •Make sure you dry your skin completely after bathing. •Avoid excessive sweating, if possible. •Make sure your shoes are dry before wearing them. •Wear clean, dry clothes. See full list on healthline.com Erythrasma can be treated. Most people respond to treatment within two to four weeks. However, it’s possible for erythrasma to become chronic and return. This is more likely to happen if you have a medical condition that affects your immune system. In general, erythrasma is a mild condition. It shouldn’t interfere with your ability to do normal activities. See full list on healthline.com Jun 15, 2026 · Erythrasma is a common bacterial skin infection that causes discolored, slightly scaly patches in skin folds, like your groin and armpits. Jun 14, 2026 · The infection causes a discolored patch, mainly in skin folds such as the armpits or groin. 1 The rash itself is not serious but may be an early warning sign of a more serious condition. The treatment may involve improved hygiene and topical or oral antibiotics if the condition is severe. Oct 20, 2022 · Involvement of the toe clefts is common, but clinically important infections present as slowly enlarging pink or brown patches on the inner thighs and groins, the axillae, and the intergluteal and submammary flexures. Skin diseases that have excessive scale or flaking (papulosquamous disorders) are due to epidermal inflammation or proliferation. We list localised and generalised scaly skin disorders by their duration and body site."}]}
