{"status": "ok", "backend": "ddgs-auto", "query": "Rheumatoid arthritis symptoms in 55yr old retired athlete", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T19:27:54.882989+00:00", "documents": [{"title": "How to tell if you have rheumatoid arthritis - Medical News Today", "url": "https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/how-do-you-know-if-you-have-rheumatoid-arthritis", "snippet": "Jul 29, 2022 · Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition where the body attacks the tissue lining the joints, causing inflammation and pain, most commonly in the hands, wrists, and knees. Early signs of..."}, {"title": "Elderly Onset Rheumatoid Arthritis: Symptoms, Treatment, MoreHealthy Aging With Rheumatoid Arthritis - WebMDRheumatoid Arthritis Symptoms : Johns Hopkins Arthritis CenterRheumatoid Arthritis in Older Adults: Understanding, Symptoms ...Rheumatoid arthritis - Symptoms and causes - Mayo ClinicRheumatoid Arthritis (RA) Symptoms and Complications - WebMD", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/rheumatoid-arthritis/elderly-onset-rheumatoid-arthritis", "snippet": "Nov 22, 2022 · Elderly onset rheumatoid arthritis is RA that's diagnosed in older adults. Learn more about its different symptoms and treatment options. May 11, 2026 · Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) can bring on challenges as you get older. There’s a greater chance of falls, along with other health problems, like heart disease and diabetes. And if you’re not able... The typical case of rheumatoid arthritis begins insidiously, with the slow development of signs and symptoms over weeks to months. Often the patient first notices stiffness in one or more joints, usually accompanied by pain on movement and by tenderness in the joint. The symptoms of rheumatoid arthritis in older adults are similar to those in younger people, but they may develop more slowly or be more difficult to recognize due to age-related factors. Apr 9, 2025 · Symptoms of rheumatoid arthritis may include: Painful, warm, swollen joints. Joint stiffness that most often is worse in the mornings and after periods of rest. It can last for 45 minutes or longer. Tiredness, fever and not wanting to eat. Rheumatoid arthritis may affect just a few joints at first. Jan 25, 2026 · Rheumatoid arthritis causes pain, swelling, and tenderness in your joints. But RA inflammation can also affect many other parts of your body and worsen your mental health."}, {"title": "Healthy Aging With Rheumatoid Arthritis - WebMD", "url": "https://www.webmd.com/rheumatoid-arthritis/healthy-aging-with-rheumatoid-arthritis", "snippet": "May 11, 2026 · Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) can bring on challenges as you get older. There’s a greater chance of falls, along with other health problems, like heart disease and diabetes. And if you’re not able..."}]}
